  "result": "Fixed: completion now keeps `#` as a normal character instead of dropping it and everything after it.\n\n**Cause:** `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py` used `shlex.shlex`, which treats `#` as a comment start by default. So `cli a#b` became `[\"cli\", \"a\"]`, and `cli #tag more` lost both `#tag` and `more`.\n\n**Fix:** I set `lex.commenters = \"\"` in `split_arg_string`.\n\n**Test:** I added two cases (`cli a#b` and `cli #tag more`) to `test_split_arg_string` in `tests/test_parser.py`. That test and `tests/test_shell_completion.py` pass (67 tests).\n\nI did not update `CHANGES.md`, which `CLAUDE.md` asks for on every user-visible change.",
